WEBVTT

00:25:25.038 --> 00:25:31.496
a reasonably good decision, not
in terms of how it turns out,

00:25:31.829 --> 00:25:36.413
but that you've been reasonably
conscientious in terms of assessing

00:25:36.413 --> 00:25:42.079
alternatives and not biasing the
data process accountability.

00:25:42.621 --> 00:25:44.954
That's a second step for
avoiding escalation.

00:25:45.079 --> 00:25:48.413
The important thing with this
is setting your targets

00:25:48.413 --> 00:25:50.454
and your benchmarks in advance.

00:25:50.954 --> 00:25:52.704
One way of holding people accountable for

00:25:52.704 --> 00:25:55.829
a good decision process is to
establish kill signals.

00:25:59.038 --> 00:26:03.954
A kill signal was a mechanism for
keeping ourselves honest,